{"caption":"Frozen Slack-Targeted Stochastic Charging Repair (STaR). The initial plan is scored on a shared 512-draw search tape. Visit priority follows the marginal isolated-wait reliability bound and gaps near the most critical visit come first. Proposals interleave quantity and topology moves. Duplicates are skipped. A newly admitted plan counts as a trial even when its deterministic check fails. The analytical screen is active only for an empirically attaining incumbent. It bounds true fixed-plan reliability, which the finite-tape estimate may exceed. The 128-draw prefix bound uses the same tape, and survivors extend to 512. The score prefers attainment. At or above target, minimize full return then maximize reliability. Below target, maximize reliability then minimize full return. A strict gain updates and restarts. Exhaustion or a guard returns the incumbent for independent validation without search feedback. Operator sketches are conceptual. New topologies use minimal and, where applicable, downstream-rate-based allocations. Letters identify stations and numbers identify customers.","dpi":400,"font":"DejaVu Sans","formats_sha256":{"pdf":"835566b0c88bf5ee457cc07bc4b4c444e3bd794a9dbce5d31d716b1e6c5416bd","png":"5621ca5a76390d31f85e95eaa7bb405e0ad78cde5d0b0b40b33df53315b1b1b8","svg":"3c66f4fc654ffad6943240623c3ef37fa1db6ec58efe59258396202594a908e3"},"physical_mm":[178.0,131.0],"plot_source_sha256":"5bd96f39fa2a67b0cb232fc49d96980263efb0fc5abd9737440b56c7ef17fb40","plotted":{"bounds":{"C_L":"(C_k + (S - k) C_0) / S","R_U":"(m + S - k) / S","full":512,"prefix":128,"prefix_completion_cushion":1e-08,"screen_tolerance":1e-12,"target":0.95},"edges":[["initialize","rank","initial feasible trace and full score"],["rank","propose","critical visits and gaps"],["propose","feasible","next unique plan within guards"],["feasible","screen","valid deterministic trace"],["screen","prefix","bypass if incumbent below empirical target, or screen passes"],["prefix","score","optimistic score strictly beats incumbent and full tape extension completes"],["score","rank","strict improvement before wall guard; update incumbent and restart"],["feasible","propose","invalid or duplicate (common retry line)"],["screen","propose","model reliability reject (common retry line)"],["prefix","propose","bound or budget reject (common retry line)"],["score","propose","no strict gain (common retry line)"],["propose","return","proposal stream exhausted or a cooperative guard stops search"],["return","validation","independent final assessment; no search feedback"],["prefix","propose","advance if full extension cannot be completed while guards permit"]],"nodes":[{"heading":"Start from original route","id":"initialize","lines":["Feasible ordered plan","Station laws, target, caps","Trace + score on 512 draws"],"source":"competitive_search.py:188\u2013224; route_evaluator.py:56\u201375, 87\u2013107"},{"heading":"Rank visits and gaps","id":"rank","lines":["Lowest upper bound first","Prioritize gaps near the","most critical station"],"source":"competitive_search.py:150\u2013158; timing.py:73\u201392"},{"heading":"Interleave moves","id":"propose","lines":["Adjust or transfer charge","Remove, replace, relocate","or insert, then allocate"],"source":"competitive_search.py:48\u2013169, 225\u2013249; charge_plan.py:49\u201373"},{"heading":"Check candidate","id":"feasible","lines":["Skip duplicate plans","Require energy feasibility","and zero-wait timing"],"source":"competitive_search.py:235\u2013250; route_evaluator.py:56\u201374; deterministic_simulator.py:166\u2013282"},{"heading":"Analytical screen","id":"screen","lines":["If incumbent attains:","reject when marginal bound","falls below target\u00b9"],"source":"competitive_search.py:251\u2013258; timing.py:73\u201392"},{"heading":"Prefix evaluation","id":"prefix","lines":["Score a 128-draw prefix","Prune if it cannot improve","Otherwise extend to 512"],"source":"competitive_search.py:259\u2013269; route_evaluator.py:76\u20